        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akira Yoshizawa, Emperor Hirohito\n- Concepts: wet-folding, Shōwa era\n- Honors: Order of the Rising Sun\n\nFacts:\n- Wet-folding is an origami technique developed by Akira Yoshizawa that uses water to dampen paper so it can be manipulated more easily.\n- In 1983, Emperor Hirohito awarded Akira Yoshizawa the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, one of Japan's highest honors.\n- Shōwa was the era name for Emperor Hirohito's reign and became his own name after his death.",
